Thank you for the outline and the answers: I start chapter 1 the wake after RP1 is signed. Round 2, read against the editor's voice and the zoom. All nine round-1 points read as he would say them now. Five small ones left; the words are yours.

1. 10-page, page 1 and page 3: the arrival is said twice, "(the first four within an hour, the rest through the day)" on page 1 and "four within the hour, the rest through the day" on page 3. A parenthesis mid-sentence is not how he writes. I would cut it from page 1, where the cast has not arrived yet, and keep page 3's. I have asked the researcher to confirm the hour on C011 (writer__003).
2. 3-page edition promises "the four steps"; the 10-page edition's last page has five. A reader who zooms in sees four become five. Either is right at its altitude, but one line in the ten would carry them across: "the same four steps, and a fifth for when you are not alone".
3. 10-page, page 7: "That is why I could let it run through the night." "It" reads as the hold. Suggested: "let them run".
4. Both series pages now say "GEN ZX FOUNDERS" in capitals; both title pages say "Gen ZX Founders". If the capitals are the series' own mark (designer__068), keep them and say so in the notes; if not, the title page's form in both.
5. 3-page, page 3, and 10-page, page 7: "sixteen minutes before the talk was due". It is the arithmetic of 18:44 and 19:00 (C010), which the bands carry; nothing to change, noted only because it is the one figure in a narrator line of both editions.

